      <rules>
        <rule id="88f0-d2a5-df80-949e" name="Special character" hidden="false">
          <description>Unique named selection. 257 points includes the complete listed fixed equipment, companions, powers and mounts; only separately offered options add points. Printed profiles are before magic-item bonuses unless a rule says they are already included. Special-character use requires the players’ agreement under the books’ convention.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="8a9f-2f2d-29a4-a3fe" name="Included equipment" hidden="false">
          <description>Light armour; Elf-biter; chariot with three Giant Wolves.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="b13a-9646-d3ee-527f" name="Price and army standard" hidden="false" publicationId="b4e3-1e3f-4601-d0dd" page="97">
          <description>80 Grom +65 Niblit +62 chariot +50 Axe =257 points. Niblit is compulsory and occupies the normal Battle Standard Bearer choice. He may buy one separate magic item, including a magic standard. Reference: Orcs &amp; Goblins, printed p. 97.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="40d4-0ab6-6cb4-895b" name="Regeneration" hidden="false" publicationId="b4e3-1e3f-4601-d0dd" page="97">
          <description>At each phase end, each wound inflicted on Grom that phase regenerates on 4+, even if he was killed. Fire wounds cannot regenerate; suffering a fire wound permanently removes this ability. Reference: Orcs &amp; Goblins, printed p. 97.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="7782-d525-5ed3-450e" name="Required unit" hidden="false">
          <description>Requires at least one of: Goblins, Goblin Wolf Riders.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
